# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/

# Tooling caches
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Flaky Test Detective's own output. History is machine-local by default; see the
# README for how to share it across a team.
.flaky.db
.flaky.db-wal
.flaky.db-shm
*.flaky.db
# `flaky demo` writes here by default. Generated data, so never committed -- and it must
# not be, or the committed copy would be the fixture this deliberately is not.
.flaky-demo.db
.flaky-demo.db-wal
.flaky-demo.db-shm
dist-check/
reports/
flaky-report.html

# Editors / OS
.DS_Store
.idea/
*.swp

# Frontend
web/node_modules/
web/dist/
web/.vite/
web/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
npm-debug.log*

# NOTE: src/flaky_detective/web/static/ is deliberately NOT ignored. Those are the
# compiled dashboard assets, committed so that `flaky serve` works from a plain
# `pip install` with no Node toolchain present. tests/test_web.py checks they are
# present and current, so a stale bundle fails the build rather than rendering a
# blank page.

# NOTE: .kiro/ is deliberately NOT ignored. The specs, steering files, and hooks
# are part of this project's record of how it was built, and the hackathon rules
# require them to be present in the repository.
